  "truthSource": "manual_audit",
  "truthReference": "Independent hand audit of validation/m12/fixtures/zig/*.zig against Zig semantics and the M11 Zig contract (validated 1.000/1.000 in M11.10; symbols only). Symbols: pub const X = struct/enum/union/error set -> struct/enum/union/enum; value constants (number/string/bool) -> constant; capitalized type aliases -> type; container fields -> property (struct/union) or enum_member (enum); error set members -> enum_member; fn inside a container -> method, at file scope -> function; pub fn/const -> visibility public, private otherwise. Noise: function-local variables (locals are execution artifacts, no symbols), control flow (while/if/switch arms), field access, keyword usage; members of an ANONYMOUS struct returned by a generic function (fn GenericStack(...) type { return struct {...} }) have no stable container identity and are NOT symbols (only the generic function itself is a symbol). Relationships (family contract, matches Java M12.01 / C M12.16 / Rust M12.18): contains = REAL container ownership only (struct/enum/union/error set -> member) — never `global contains X`; no References edge for @import (imports stay in the imports array — Rust M12.18 contract, no dangling `references root -> module`); no generic `exports module -> X` edge (module is not a symbol; the exports array and pub visibility carry the export fact); no phantom switch edge (switch is a keyword, never a symbol); calls/uses/instantiates are not emitted in this contract set (Zig method dispatch via field access is an execution artifact). Relationship sources are container names; top-level symbols have no contains edge.",
